        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "VCC : C1.1(passive) C3.1(passive) ... Q1.2(S,passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "C3 | 100nF | Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric | Device:C_Small"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "When Q2 pulls Q1's gate low, C3 can hold the gate near that voltage after Q2 turns off. Q1 may remain on or behave unpredictably instead of reliably switching the fan supply off.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U2", "U3"],
      "pins": ["U2.1", "U3.1", "U2.5", "U3.5", "U2.6", "U3.6", "U2.7", "U3.7", "U2.2", "U3.2", "U2.3", "U3.3", "U2.4", "U3.4", "U2.8", "U3.8"],
      "nets": ["RST", "SDA", "PWM", "SCK", "POT", "TACH", "GND", "+5V"],
      "observed": "Both the ATtiny45 (U2) and ATtiny13 (U3) are connected in parallel on their corresponding supply, reset, and I/O pins, including their PWM outputs.",
      "expected": "The board should use one controller, or provide isolation/selection so two populated MCUs do not drive the same nets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "PWM : J4.1(MISO,passive) R2.1(passive) R5.2(passive) U2.6(PB1,bidirectional) U3.6(PB1,bidirectional)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "SDA : J1.2(Pin_2,passive) J4.4(MOSI,passive) U2.5(AREF/PB0,bidirectional) U3.5(PB0,bidirectional)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "+5V : ... U2.8(VCC,power_in) U3.8(VCC,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND : ... U2.4(GND,power_in) U3.4(GND,power_in)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both listed MCUs are populated, they can contend on shared outputs and may execute different firmware, making controller operation unreliable or causing electrical stress.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The PMOS fan-supply switch lacks a DC gate pull-up, so its off state is not reliable. The netlist also connects two powered MCUs in parallel on their control and I/O nets, which is unsafe if both are populated."
}

